1
00:00:00,880 --> 00:00:03,880
Then it wasn't just some old folktale after all!

2
00:00:04,080 --> 00:00:07,260
The ancient kingdom they said was destroyed really did exist!

3
00:00:09,620 --> 00:00:11,420
This gold's the real deal.

4
00:00:11,740 --> 00:00:12,960
This is incredible.

5
00:00:13,360 --> 00:00:13,600
Hey.

6
00:00:15,120 --> 00:00:17,440
I think we should all go back up to the surface.

7
00:00:17,860 --> 00:00:20,380
If we're gonna explore, we should prep first, don't you think?

8
00:00:20,860 --> 00:00:23,320
Wait, what's all this nonsense you're spouting?

9
00:00:23,500 --> 00:00:27,500
Senshi, are you sure you've got iron running through your veins like the rest of us?

10
00:00:27,620 --> 00:00:28,640
Don't push yourself.

11
00:00:28,640 --> 00:00:30,480
You can stay here if you want.

12
00:00:31,700 --> 00:00:33,300
No, I want gold too!

13
00:00:34,300 --> 00:00:37,300
I was afraid to be left alone, so I lied.

14
00:00:38,120 --> 00:00:39,880
I really didn't like that place.

15
00:00:40,300 --> 00:00:46,380
And to make matters worse, my normally ambitious party members started acting a bit too ambitious.

16
00:00:47,140 --> 00:00:51,020
As we went deeper and deeper, their eyes seemed to glow in the darkness.

17
00:00:51,700 --> 00:00:54,120
It was like they were being drawn in by something.

18
00:00:54,120 --> 00:00:58,220
Then suddenly, the nightmare began.

19
00:00:58,640 --> 00:01:01,920
What happened?

20
00:01:01,920 --> 00:01:05,260
It was a monster.

21
00:01:06,420 --> 00:01:08,720
This huge bird-like thing came from out of nowhere.

22
00:01:09,340 --> 00:01:11,140
Then it killed poor Toton.

23
00:01:11,780 --> 00:01:14,800
These ruins, they've evolved into a dungeon.

24
00:01:14,800 --> 00:01:22,000
The fear finally snapped them out of their trance, but by then, we didn't know how to find our way back.

25
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:25,920
We're not trapped in here, are we?

26
00:01:25,920 --> 00:01:31,080
Dungeons are always linked to the surface, so there's gotta be a way out.

27
00:01:31,080 --> 00:01:33,580
Let's calm down and search for the exit.

28
00:01:33,580 --> 00:01:39,740
We wandered the dungeon, doing our best to avoid any monsters, but it was odd.

29
00:01:39,740 --> 00:01:42,620
When we got thirsty, there'd be a spring.

30
00:01:42,620 --> 00:01:46,540
When we got tired, a room where we could rest would appear.

31
00:01:46,540 --> 00:01:51,420
One person even said a woman would try to seduce them from the shadows.

32
00:01:51,420 --> 00:01:55,340
Eventually, we ran out of rations.

33
00:01:55,340 --> 00:01:58,140
We'll die from starvation at this rate.

34
00:01:58,140 --> 00:02:01,340
We gotta find food, even if that means fighting for it.

35
00:02:01,340 --> 00:02:02,300
What do you mean?

36
00:02:02,960 --> 00:02:05,660
Basically, at this point, we gotta eat or be eaten.

37
00:02:06,380 --> 00:02:10,260
Invar, Brigand, I want both of you to take shields and be our defense.

38
00:02:10,840 --> 00:02:13,620
Nala and I will use our weapons to push the monsters back.

39
00:02:13,980 --> 00:02:18,000
And Senshi, you stay right here and make a detailed map of the area.

40
00:02:19,780 --> 00:02:20,560
Move out!

41
00:02:20,560 --> 00:02:29,800
That bird monster showed up again.

42
00:02:29,800 --> 00:02:33,100
That bastard always taking flight to get away.

43
00:02:34,900 --> 00:02:37,160
I'll go with you next time you search for food.

44
00:02:37,540 --> 00:02:39,560
Enough! You're only getting away.

45
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:41,740
I've already found some food.

46
00:02:42,140 --> 00:02:42,980
Eat your fill of it.

47
00:02:44,240 --> 00:02:48,860
I felt awful for getting hungry, even though I never did anything.

48
00:02:48,860 --> 00:02:54,000
Our days became a desperate search for food instead of a way to the surface.

49
00:02:54,840 --> 00:02:57,000
The bird continued to chase us relentlessly.

50
00:02:58,020 --> 00:03:00,180
Every time we fought it, we'd lose someone.

51
00:03:00,840 --> 00:03:04,180
Now pressed for food, we were forced to eat our horse.

52
00:03:05,480 --> 00:03:08,320
A four-legged eagle, no doubt about it.

53
00:03:08,780 --> 00:03:10,840
That bird monster is a griffon.

54
00:03:11,180 --> 00:03:13,280
Why does it have such a grudge against us?

55
00:03:13,620 --> 00:03:15,560
Doesn't even seem like it's all that hungry.

56
00:03:15,560 --> 00:03:18,760
I reckon because it probably enjoys killing.

57
00:03:19,260 --> 00:03:22,200
It's just part of a monster's natural instinct, I suppose.

58
00:03:22,200 --> 00:03:25,560
But don't you worry.

59
00:03:25,840 --> 00:03:28,840
The next time it shows up, we're gonna roast it whole and eat it.

60
00:03:29,340 --> 00:03:29,740
Here.

61
00:03:30,300 --> 00:03:32,620
Give thanks for the meat and provide it and eat up.

62
00:03:32,620 --> 00:03:37,720
What the hell are you thinking, Dylan?

63
00:03:38,000 --> 00:03:41,400
You gave most of the food we had left to that good-for-nothing kid.

64
00:03:41,500 --> 00:03:43,640
He's only 36 and still growing.

65
00:03:43,760 --> 00:03:44,780
He needs all he can get.

66
00:03:45,040 --> 00:03:48,100
It's our responsibility as adults to take care of the young'uns.

67
00:03:48,120 --> 00:03:49,540
Now's not the time for that.

68
00:03:49,600 --> 00:03:53,540
Then what good are we if we can't even nurture the next generation of dwarves?

69
00:03:53,540 --> 00:04:06,160
I'm so hungry.

70
00:04:06,820 --> 00:04:11,560
If there really is iron flowing through my veins, then surely I can eat these rocks.

71
00:04:12,120 --> 00:04:12,680
Hey!

72
00:04:13,020 --> 00:04:16,260
You're hiding some food from the sharks, you damn it!

73
00:04:16,740 --> 00:04:18,040
What do you think you're doing?

74
00:04:18,360 --> 00:04:19,400
It's his fault!

75
00:04:19,400 --> 00:04:23,720
Let's take this outside, since she looks pretty scared.

76
00:04:24,820 --> 00:04:26,220
I'm sick of this!

77
00:04:26,420 --> 00:04:29,140
The yelling gradually got more and more intense.

78
00:04:29,480 --> 00:04:33,160
I heard sounds of fighting and suddenly some horrifying screams.

79
00:04:33,160 --> 00:04:33,660
Ah!

80
00:04:36,340 --> 00:04:43,240
After that, it became eerily quiet.

81
00:04:44,760 --> 00:04:46,260
What happened up there?

82
00:04:46,560 --> 00:04:47,340
Where's Brigand?

83
00:04:47,580 --> 00:04:48,640
Enough questions.

84
00:04:49,400 --> 00:04:51,360
You shouldn't look outside.

85
00:04:52,260 --> 00:04:54,480
We both got attacked by the griffon.

86
00:04:54,960 --> 00:04:59,100
I managed to land the killing blow on it, but Brigand wasn't so lucky.

87
00:04:59,480 --> 00:05:05,320
When I looked at Giland's helmet, there was a dent in it that looked like he got struck with a blunt weapon.

88
00:05:06,320 --> 00:05:08,080
Let's start cooking that griffon.

89
00:05:08,700 --> 00:05:13,520
If we cut it up and make soup out of it, we can last a few more days.

90
00:05:13,520 --> 00:05:28,220
The griffon soup was just meat boiled in water.

91
00:05:28,220 --> 00:05:32,640
The flavor itself was horrible due to the smell and toughness of the meat.

92
00:05:32,640 --> 00:05:37,100
But I couldn't stop eating.

93
00:05:37,100 --> 00:05:40,780
I chewed and chewed, taking my time to finish it.

94
00:05:40,780 --> 00:05:46,480
Gilland said he needed to take a leak, then slowly staggered outside.

95
00:05:46,480 --> 00:05:51,760
He never walked back through that door.

96
00:05:51,760 --> 00:05:54,880
I had been left there, all alone.

97
00:05:54,880 --> 00:05:58,840
I didn't have the courage to try to venture outside the room.

98
00:05:58,840 --> 00:06:08,300
I couldn't bring myself to leave, but I rationed out the rest of the meat and closely studied all the maps I'd drawn up until then.

99
00:06:08,300 --> 00:06:15,920
Eventually, I figured out the rules of the codes written on the walls, and once I felt ready, I finally left the room.

100
00:06:19,820 --> 00:06:21,340
There weren't any corpses.

101
00:06:22,340 --> 00:06:26,340
Some critters must have come by in search of food and picked everything clean.

102
00:06:27,220 --> 00:06:32,860
After I left, I was captured by the orcs, and they confined me as a prisoner in their settlement for a while.

103
00:06:32,860 --> 00:06:39,360
But I got to know them, and learned they were a good-natured bunch, in exchange for teaching them ancient Dwarvish.

104
00:06:39,360 --> 00:06:45,700
They taught me how to identify which mushrooms I could and couldn't eat, and how to hold my own against monsters.

105
00:06:47,000 --> 00:06:49,360
And with that knowledge...

106
00:06:49,360 --> 00:06:57,200
I managed to get back up to the surface.

107
00:06:57,200 --> 00:07:04,000
But when I thought about everything that had happened in the dungeon, I couldn't bring myself to return to my homeland.

108
00:07:05,100 --> 00:07:07,880
I lived around the dungeon and its shallower levels.

109
00:07:08,600 --> 00:07:14,240
It wasn't too long before the dungeon became connected to the town, and lots of adventurers started to pass through.

110
00:07:15,040 --> 00:07:21,020
I had so much anxiety over whether or not it was griffin meat in that soup I had all that time ago.

111
00:07:21,020 --> 00:07:25,440
Well, every time I ate something, I'd remember that distinct flavor.

112
00:07:26,180 --> 00:07:30,420
All the monster meat I've eaten so far has never even come close to how it tasted.

113
00:07:31,220 --> 00:07:34,420
And that's the reason why I ran away from the griffin earlier.

114
00:07:36,380 --> 00:07:39,940
I'm afraid to finally learn the truth.

115
00:07:40,840 --> 00:07:41,840
How horrible.

116
00:07:43,200 --> 00:07:43,640
Senshi.

117
00:07:45,400 --> 00:07:47,480
Well, we got that, griffin. You want to eat it?

118
00:07:47,480 --> 00:07:51,080
I, uh, just thought it might help.

119
00:07:51,200 --> 00:07:54,500
You don't want to have all that in the back of your head for the rest of your life, do you?

120
00:07:54,880 --> 00:07:56,580
If it's the same, you can relax.

121
00:07:56,800 --> 00:08:00,220
But if it's a completely different flavor, then that sucks.

122
00:08:00,660 --> 00:08:02,060
But at least you would have an answer.

123
00:08:02,400 --> 00:08:03,760
That's a terrible plan.

124
00:08:04,260 --> 00:08:05,400
Is this guy serious?

125
00:08:06,280 --> 00:08:07,800
It's your call, Senshi.

126
00:08:11,300 --> 00:08:13,860
You're right, Laios. Guess I should try some.

127
00:08:14,480 --> 00:08:15,580
Are you sure?

128
00:08:15,580 --> 00:08:17,560
All right.

129
00:08:17,860 --> 00:08:21,180
In that case, let's do our best to recreate Senshi's soup.

130
00:08:21,520 --> 00:08:23,360
And we'll start by slicing off some meat.

131
00:08:23,860 --> 00:08:26,920
The top half and bottom half taste totally different from each other.

132
00:08:27,180 --> 00:08:28,320
So let's grab both.

133
00:08:28,520 --> 00:08:29,920
You just want to eat both.

134
00:08:34,440 --> 00:08:35,900
Such amazing muscles.

135
00:08:36,480 --> 00:08:37,660
A typical carnivore.

136
00:08:38,540 --> 00:08:41,400
I wonder why that other one kept pursuing Senshi's party.

137
00:08:41,400 --> 00:08:45,120
It killed them, but it didn't care about eating them.

138
00:08:45,680 --> 00:08:47,800
Oh, you mentioned you had a horse, right?

139
00:08:48,220 --> 00:08:48,900
Did you know?

140
00:08:49,320 --> 00:08:51,080
They're a griffin's favorite thing to eat.

141
00:08:51,700 --> 00:08:54,080
So then why didn't it go after the horse first?

142
00:08:54,340 --> 00:08:54,880
Don't know.

143
00:08:54,880 --> 00:08:57,600
I'll go boil some water.

144
00:08:59,300 --> 00:09:02,660
A griffin's weapons are its front claws and its beak.

145
00:09:02,920 --> 00:09:05,980
But neither of those things would have left a dent in a helmet like that.

146
00:09:06,480 --> 00:09:09,760
So whatever attacked Gillen most likely wasn't a griffin.

147
00:09:10,660 --> 00:09:13,020
With that said, what about the others?

148
00:09:14,020 --> 00:09:16,340
Marcila and I mistook Fallon for a griffin,

149
00:09:16,520 --> 00:09:18,540
so Senshi's party could have been wrong too.

150
00:09:18,540 --> 00:09:22,160
After all, there are several large monsters that have wings.

151
00:09:22,960 --> 00:09:28,360
Cockatrice, Basilisk, Harpy, Siren, Pegasus, Simurg, Rock.

152
00:09:29,300 --> 00:09:32,320
Out of those, which one could attack with blunt force?

153
00:09:33,080 --> 00:09:34,940
The water's boiling now.

154
00:09:35,940 --> 00:09:37,380
We just boil it?

155
00:09:37,840 --> 00:09:38,840
Should we add anything?

156
00:09:39,440 --> 00:09:40,400
No, that's it.

157
00:09:41,040 --> 00:09:42,980
It'll be a flavorless soup, though.

158
00:09:43,780 --> 00:09:45,320
Maybe I could garnish it.

159
00:09:45,320 --> 00:09:47,500
Come to think of it,

160
00:09:47,760 --> 00:09:50,660
you said the orcs taught you how to differentiate mushrooms, right?

161
00:09:51,120 --> 00:09:52,520
Have you ever seen those before?

162
00:09:53,000 --> 00:09:54,660
Nope. Those are new to me.

163
00:09:57,100 --> 00:09:58,980
Marcel, you got this, right?

164
00:09:59,800 --> 00:10:02,960
Hey! You come this far and then just dump it on me?

165
00:10:03,120 --> 00:10:04,140
What's wrong with you?

166
00:10:04,920 --> 00:10:06,180
Whatever, we're done here.

167
00:10:06,440 --> 00:10:08,080
Even if we do this, Senshi isn't...

168
00:10:08,080 --> 00:10:08,320
No.

169
00:10:09,080 --> 00:10:11,120
We went through the trouble, so I'll eat it.

170
00:10:11,600 --> 00:10:13,920
I'll accept the results no matter what they are.

171
00:10:15,320 --> 00:10:22,960
It's ready.

172
00:10:22,960 --> 00:10:23,040
It's ready.

173
00:10:29,760 --> 00:10:31,260
This flavor...

174
00:10:31,260 --> 00:10:34,220
It's nothing at all like what I tasted back then.

175
00:10:37,220 --> 00:10:39,800
I guess it's exactly what I feared it was.

176
00:10:41,100 --> 00:10:42,280
Senshi, I...

177
00:10:42,280 --> 00:10:43,000
It's fine.

178
00:10:43,000 --> 00:10:44,880
At least I know now.

179
00:10:45,840 --> 00:10:48,460
Gillen wanted me to survive no matter what the cost.

180
00:10:48,940 --> 00:10:52,180
So, I'll carry that with me for the rest of my life.

181
00:10:52,840 --> 00:10:54,120
Miles, you big idiot!

182
00:10:54,340 --> 00:10:55,760
You just traumatized some more!

183
00:10:58,320 --> 00:11:00,080
Griffin meat smells gamey.

184
00:11:00,300 --> 00:11:02,260
And the texture of it makes it hard to chew.

185
00:11:02,540 --> 00:11:04,400
The worst part's the bad aftertaste.

186
00:11:04,400 --> 00:11:10,040
So, what Senshi had eaten back then wasn't actually Griffin.

187
00:11:10,040 --> 00:11:13,260
And it definitely wasn't human.

188
00:11:13,260 --> 00:11:16,000
The monster that attacked them was a hippogriff.

189
00:11:16,260 --> 00:11:17,140
I'm sure of it.

190
00:11:17,760 --> 00:11:18,860
So, what's the difference?

191
00:11:19,540 --> 00:11:23,320
A griffin's lower half is a lion, while a hippogriff's is more horse-like.

192
00:11:23,880 --> 00:11:26,780
The one from back then must have been after Senshi's horse.

193
00:11:27,240 --> 00:11:29,380
It was either curious about it or was in heat.

194
00:11:29,380 --> 00:11:32,940
Also, hippogriffs have something that griffins don't have.

195
00:11:33,340 --> 00:11:35,360
And that's hind legs with hooves.

196
00:11:35,840 --> 00:11:37,200
It's over if you get kicked.

197
00:11:37,620 --> 00:11:40,220
The kick's so strong, it'd even dent metal.

198
00:11:40,220 --> 00:11:43,220
And there you have it, Senshi.

199
00:11:43,720 --> 00:11:46,120
If what you'd eaten before was really a hippogriff,

200
00:11:46,500 --> 00:11:49,020
then of course this soup has a completely different flavor.

201
00:11:52,740 --> 00:11:54,440
I appreciate it, Laios.

202
00:11:55,200 --> 00:11:57,300
Hearing that does ease my mind a bit.

203
00:11:58,300 --> 00:12:01,280
Even if there's no way to know how a hippogriff tastes.

204
00:12:03,780 --> 00:12:05,400
Well then, why don't we find out?

205
00:12:05,940 --> 00:12:06,300
Huh?

206
00:12:06,700 --> 00:12:09,300
Let's compare this with the taste of some hippogriff meat.

207
00:12:09,300 --> 00:12:11,080
Hey, wait a minute!

208
00:12:11,460 --> 00:12:12,460
Aren't you supposed to say,

209
00:12:12,560 --> 00:12:13,740
the truth is still unknown,

210
00:12:13,860 --> 00:12:16,000
but at least there's a ray of hope and end it there?

211
00:12:16,200 --> 00:12:18,600
Laios, do you even know where to find a hippogriff?

212
00:12:19,600 --> 00:12:20,440
Of course.

213
00:12:20,940 --> 00:12:22,860
There's one right under our noses!

214
00:12:23,540 --> 00:12:26,120
Previously, there's been sightings of them in this dungeon.

215
00:12:26,500 --> 00:12:28,740
And there's something we should have realized sooner.

216
00:12:29,320 --> 00:12:32,420
We defeated a griffin that was never reported to even be here.

217
00:12:32,800 --> 00:12:33,460
Why's that?

218
00:12:33,740 --> 00:12:37,160
It's because there was an accomplice that helped complicate the situation.

219
00:12:37,800 --> 00:12:39,040
An accomplice?

220
00:12:39,300 --> 00:12:41,480
The changelings.

221
00:12:42,920 --> 00:12:46,260
There's a related folktale that derives from your birthplace, Chilchuk.

222
00:12:47,080 --> 00:12:49,020
Have you ever heard of the replacement child?

223
00:12:49,660 --> 00:12:51,880
It's when a child gets replaced with a monster.

224
00:12:52,560 --> 00:12:57,340
A child will go out to play in the woods and return looking like a troll version of themselves.

225
00:12:57,340 --> 00:13:00,480
For a while, people thought it was some kind of magic.

226
00:13:00,480 --> 00:13:04,740
But only recently discovered that it was because of these mushroom-shaped monsters.

227
00:13:05,440 --> 00:13:09,500
Any creature who steps into a ring of them will end up changing just a little bit.

228
00:13:09,500 --> 00:13:14,300
Once people realized that, they got rid of them, so they're rare now.

229
00:13:14,300 --> 00:13:16,220
But to think they'd grow here.

230
00:13:16,720 --> 00:13:19,180
The way it grabbed Senshi but didn't eat him.

231
00:13:19,480 --> 00:13:21,780
The way it kicked and killed Marcil's familiar.

232
00:13:22,800 --> 00:13:25,600
I'm almost positive this monster isn't actually a griffin.

233
00:13:25,600 --> 00:13:28,060
Time to find out.

234
00:13:29,060 --> 00:13:32,740
Take the griffin meat and place it inside the changeling's fairy ring.

235
00:13:35,620 --> 00:13:37,380
It's totally different now.

236
00:13:37,620 --> 00:13:39,580
It looks even tastier with the marbling.

237
00:13:39,580 --> 00:13:42,100
All right, let's make some soup.

238
00:14:06,900 --> 00:14:07,500
Senshi!

239
00:14:07,500 --> 00:14:13,360
Uh, well, flavors can change pretty drastically based on certain conditions, so...

240
00:14:13,360 --> 00:14:13,680
No.

241
00:14:14,480 --> 00:14:15,720
It's not that.

242
00:14:17,360 --> 00:14:18,500
It's just...

243
00:14:19,100 --> 00:14:22,260
I've always dreamed of drinking the soup again one day.

244
00:14:26,420 --> 00:14:28,680
Thank you, everyone.

245
00:14:30,760 --> 00:14:31,700
Thank you.

246
00:14:31,700 --> 00:14:39,000
You know, living in this place for as long as I have has shown me something.

247
00:14:39,960 --> 00:14:43,400
This dungeon has a strong response to human greed and desires.

248
00:14:44,400 --> 00:14:44,800
Fortune.

249
00:14:45,360 --> 00:14:45,760
Knowledge.

250
00:14:46,400 --> 00:14:46,780
Fame.

251
00:14:46,780 --> 00:14:52,560
It tends to be a lot more lenient towards those who don't ask anything of it, like the orcs.

252
00:14:53,240 --> 00:14:56,560
Once you want something from this place, it bears its fangs.

253
00:14:57,120 --> 00:15:01,660
From this point onward, on top of trying to save Valon so you can bring her back,

254
00:15:02,080 --> 00:15:06,320
you're all gonna want to find the mad mage and the winged lion so you can break the spell.

255
00:15:06,320 --> 00:15:09,980
Well, the dungeon's sure to get even more ruthless towards you.

256
00:15:11,320 --> 00:15:15,980
Regardless, there's still plenty of things I'd like to teach you to help you reach those goals.

257
00:15:16,480 --> 00:15:18,980
So, will you let me keep tagging along?

258
00:15:18,980 --> 00:15:21,440
Of course, please do.

259
00:15:25,820 --> 00:15:26,420
Right.

260
00:15:26,720 --> 00:15:29,120
Now that that's over, let's keep moving.

261
00:15:36,580 --> 00:15:39,120
How is everyone feeling?

262
00:15:40,440 --> 00:15:41,040
Reason.

263
00:15:41,360 --> 00:15:42,260
I'm dying.

264
00:15:42,900 --> 00:15:45,460
What else could this be but food poisoning?

265
00:15:46,040 --> 00:15:48,700
We've eaten all sorts of different stuff up to now.

266
00:15:48,980 --> 00:15:52,220
But we can't let something like this be the end of us.

267
00:15:53,400 --> 00:15:54,200
Valon.

268
00:15:57,800 --> 00:15:59,480
How long did I sleep?

269
00:15:59,820 --> 00:16:00,640
I feel lighter.

270
00:16:01,460 --> 00:16:02,960
Guess the food poisoning passed.

271
00:16:03,760 --> 00:16:04,600
Thank goodness.

272
00:16:04,900 --> 00:16:06,020
I thought we were gonna die.

273
00:16:09,520 --> 00:16:10,900
What's going on?

274
00:16:11,940 --> 00:16:12,800
Oh, Marcel!

275
00:16:13,360 --> 00:16:14,480
Do you see this?

276
00:16:14,480 --> 00:16:16,000
I definitely shrunk, right?

277
00:16:18,980 --> 00:16:22,380
Wait, she shrunk too?

278
00:16:22,800 --> 00:16:24,940
Hey, Senshi, we've got a huge problem here.

279
00:16:25,040 --> 00:16:25,380
Wake!

280
00:16:27,160 --> 00:16:28,600
Who are you?

281
00:16:28,600 --> 00:16:32,300
Oh, why the hell are you guys so noisy?

282
00:16:33,020 --> 00:16:33,540
Chill.

283
00:16:34,680 --> 00:16:36,480
Mr. Chill Chuck, sir?

284
00:16:37,260 --> 00:16:44,840
From the looks of it, we accidentally ended up stepping inside the changeling ring.

285
00:16:44,840 --> 00:16:47,520
But of all things, why this?

286
00:16:47,520 --> 00:16:52,600
It changed a hippogriff into a griffon, so this isn't too out of the ordinary.

287
00:16:53,460 --> 00:16:54,440
I'm a dwarf now.

288
00:16:55,020 --> 00:16:56,060
Senshi is an elf.

289
00:16:56,680 --> 00:16:58,520
Marcille is a half foot.

290
00:16:59,200 --> 00:17:00,480
Chill Chuck is a tall man.

291
00:17:01,340 --> 00:17:04,020
And Izutsumi is a dog.

292
00:17:04,020 --> 00:17:06,500
I mean, she's probably a kobold.

293
00:17:06,720 --> 00:17:08,200
Oh, yeah, with cat ears.

294
00:17:09,020 --> 00:17:12,340
So, how do we return to our normal bodies?

295
00:17:12,960 --> 00:17:15,360
Maybe we can go back the same way we came.

296
00:17:15,720 --> 00:17:18,240
If we step inside the ring again, it might reverse, right?

297
00:17:18,620 --> 00:17:20,160
Yeah, that's what I was thinking.

298
00:17:20,500 --> 00:17:21,500
But look outside.

299
00:17:22,300 --> 00:17:24,100
Oh, the path is different now.

300
00:17:24,780 --> 00:17:27,540
While we were trying to sleep, our bodies kept shaking.

301
00:17:27,980 --> 00:17:30,260
But it was really the dungeon shifting instead?

302
00:17:30,260 --> 00:17:34,340
I don't know if this is the way we came, but let's try to head back.

303
00:17:39,180 --> 00:17:41,040
My luggage feels so light.

304
00:17:42,360 --> 00:17:44,120
Marcille, let me help you with that.

305
00:17:44,700 --> 00:17:45,900
Thank you, Laios.

306
00:17:46,420 --> 00:17:47,860
This body is great.

307
00:17:48,080 --> 00:17:49,960
I can still see even though it's dark.

308
00:17:50,220 --> 00:17:52,580
And I could probably beat Namaari in arm wrestling.

309
00:17:53,160 --> 00:17:54,080
How are you feeling?

310
00:17:54,340 --> 00:17:55,060
Everything good?

311
00:17:56,320 --> 00:18:00,240
This body's heavy, and it feels like I'm engulfed in some kind of thick curtain.

312
00:18:00,860 --> 00:18:03,240
I'm guessing your senses got a lot duller.

313
00:18:03,640 --> 00:18:04,080
Yeah.

314
00:18:04,600 --> 00:18:07,260
And I strangely feel calmer than I did before.

315
00:18:07,720 --> 00:18:11,340
Well, either way, it's nice to look down on you guys.

316
00:18:11,340 --> 00:18:23,940
Wait, isn't this...

317
00:18:23,940 --> 00:18:37,940
Wait, isn't this...

318
00:18:37,940 --> 00:18:44,380
Ah, so now we find this door?

319
00:18:44,720 --> 00:18:46,120
This takes us deeper, huh?

320
00:18:46,360 --> 00:18:49,440
We were trying to go back, but ended up moving forward anyway.

321
00:18:49,440 --> 00:18:52,160
Someone camped here.

322
00:18:52,740 --> 00:18:55,080
That means other adventurers have been by.

323
00:18:55,720 --> 00:18:59,280
Laios, do you think whoever was here might know how to fix this?

324
00:19:01,080 --> 00:19:03,500
I'm gonna guess that they didn't go through this door.

325
00:19:03,860 --> 00:19:06,320
I think they used a teleportation spell to leave.

326
00:19:06,660 --> 00:19:08,860
Oh, then what do we do?

327
00:19:09,200 --> 00:19:10,700
I've been thinking about that.

328
00:19:11,100 --> 00:19:13,300
Maybe we see if we can find the winged lion.

329
00:19:13,720 --> 00:19:14,020
Huh?

330
00:19:14,800 --> 00:19:18,180
Doesn't seem like the dungeon has any intention of letting us go yet.

331
00:19:18,500 --> 00:19:22,640
So instead of us trying to fight it, it's probably better if we move forward.

332
00:19:23,340 --> 00:19:26,920
And, I mean, once we're back on the surface, it'll be easy to fix this.

333
00:19:27,100 --> 00:19:29,020
I'm not saying we should stay like this forever.

334
00:19:29,200 --> 00:19:30,040
Are you an idiot?

335
00:19:30,200 --> 00:19:32,960
You don't care because you got turned into a long-living race.

336
00:19:33,200 --> 00:19:34,140
He's right, though.

337
00:19:34,780 --> 00:19:37,500
These bodies haven't been that inconvenient so far.

338
00:19:37,720 --> 00:19:40,420
Is a change in ear size really so concerning?

339
00:19:40,420 --> 00:19:40,820
Ah.

340
00:19:40,820 --> 00:19:47,380
Okay, so if we're gonna move forward, what are we supposed to do about this door?

341
00:19:47,720 --> 00:19:49,900
Everyone's making a fuss because it won't open, right?

342
00:19:50,400 --> 00:19:52,020
Think you can pick the lock, Chilchuk?

343
00:19:52,860 --> 00:19:55,540
I can't do it if there's no physical lock.

344
00:19:55,980 --> 00:19:57,640
I'm guessing it's locked with magic.

345
00:19:58,720 --> 00:20:04,100
I do sense magic flowing through it, although I'd need time, money, and tools to decipher it.

346
00:20:05,960 --> 00:20:09,240
John! Can you hear me? What do we do now?

347
00:20:09,240 --> 00:20:12,320
Please, Mr. Winked Lion, we need your help!

348
00:20:12,980 --> 00:20:14,760
Lyos, your stupid sword!

349
00:20:14,920 --> 00:20:16,740
There's something coming out of it!

350
00:20:18,400 --> 00:20:18,800
Kensuke?

351
00:20:19,660 --> 00:20:21,040
Wait, did it get bigger?

352
00:20:21,760 --> 00:20:24,740
I thought being in the cold for so long killed him.

353
00:20:31,160 --> 00:20:32,800
The door is...

354
00:20:32,800 --> 00:20:36,140
So do you think this means the Winked Lion is trying to help us out?

355
00:20:36,340 --> 00:20:38,160
Well, it could be him or Yad, I guess.

356
00:20:38,160 --> 00:20:39,920
We should say thanks regardless.

357
00:20:40,600 --> 00:20:41,860
We thank you!

358
00:20:42,040 --> 00:20:43,760
Whether you're the Winked Lion or Yad!

359
00:20:46,420 --> 00:20:48,760
Hey! I just heard something move!

360
00:20:49,200 --> 00:20:49,620
Huh?

361
00:20:56,800 --> 00:20:58,660
Oh, those are gargoyles!

362
00:20:59,540 --> 00:21:00,660
Prepare yourselves!

363
00:21:01,180 --> 00:21:03,000
Gargoyles are moving stone statues.

364
00:21:03,560 --> 00:21:06,100
Hit them, and you're the one who'll get hurt, so be careful!

365
00:21:06,100 --> 00:21:08,960
Looks like I'm useless here.

366
00:21:09,400 --> 00:21:11,320
I'm just gonna stay out of the way.

367
00:21:14,380 --> 00:21:16,540
What? Why the hell is it chasing me?

368
00:21:16,580 --> 00:21:18,460
Because you're the one who stands out most!

369
00:21:18,720 --> 00:21:20,140
You're tall now, dumbass!

370
00:21:20,160 --> 00:21:21,240
You need to fight, too!

371
00:21:21,320 --> 00:21:22,420
You gotta be joking!

372
00:21:22,620 --> 00:21:22,980
I...

373
00:21:22,980 --> 00:21:26,720
Chilchuk!

374
00:21:27,660 --> 00:21:28,580
He'll be fine!

375
00:21:28,780 --> 00:21:29,740
It didn't even hit!

376
00:21:33,500 --> 00:21:34,680
Wait, what happened?

377
00:21:35,160 --> 00:21:37,920
Wow, there's so many pretty rainbows in here.

378
00:21:37,920 --> 00:21:40,220
Is this mana sickness from one spell?

379
00:21:40,560 --> 00:21:41,700
This isn't good.

380
00:21:42,080 --> 00:21:44,120
Izutsumi, I need you to...

381
00:21:44,120 --> 00:21:48,140
Stay, Izutsumi!

382
00:21:48,600 --> 00:21:50,380
Don't move until I tell you to!

383
00:21:50,820 --> 00:21:53,220
The noise and smell of blood have her all wound up.

384
00:21:53,580 --> 00:21:56,000
If she attacks, she won't stop till one of them's dead.

385
00:21:56,620 --> 00:21:57,980
Senchi! Use your...

386
00:21:57,980 --> 00:22:00,620
Hey, uh...

387
00:22:00,620 --> 00:22:02,100
Why don't you have your pan?

388
00:22:02,360 --> 00:22:03,460
Because it's heavy.

389
00:22:03,460 --> 00:22:08,480
It's fine.

390
00:22:08,680 --> 00:22:10,660
My sword and the pan are much lighter now.

391
00:22:10,980 --> 00:22:13,020
In this state, I can beat them myself.

392
00:22:13,560 --> 00:22:15,500
Although, to be honest,

393
00:22:15,820 --> 00:22:18,220
with this body, I'm getting tired faster.

394
00:22:19,020 --> 00:22:19,960
Oh, no.

395
00:22:20,800 --> 00:22:22,460
We're going to lose here.

396
00:22:23,280 --> 00:22:24,820
All right, we gotta run for it.

397
00:22:25,420 --> 00:22:27,440
Senchi, you take my cell and get through the door.

398
00:22:28,160 --> 00:22:29,080
Look, he's Izutsumi.

399
00:22:29,380 --> 00:22:30,100
See this, yeah?

400
00:22:30,380 --> 00:22:31,140
Face the bell!

401
00:22:31,140 --> 00:22:34,060
Zilchuk, here!

402
00:22:34,280 --> 00:22:35,140
Use the pan lid!

403
00:22:36,260 --> 00:22:37,120
Start running!

404
00:22:37,120 --> 00:22:37,560
Zilchuk!

405
00:22:37,560 --> 00:22:38,120
Zilchuk!

406
00:22:50,120 --> 00:22:51,580
What do we do?

407
00:22:52,240 --> 00:22:54,840
These bodies are an inconvenience, after all.

408
00:22:55,560 --> 00:22:57,400
I'm starting to regret my decision.

409
00:22:58,020 --> 00:22:59,340
It can't be helped now.

410
00:22:59,340 --> 00:23:03,180
We just have to pray that we'll find some of those mushrooms up ahead.

411
00:23:07,900 --> 00:23:10,680
Yep, these are genuine dwarven ruins, all right.

412
00:23:11,280 --> 00:23:14,640
Uh, you think those mushrooms grow in a place like this?

413
00:23:14,780 --> 00:23:16,240
It's really hot in here.

414
00:23:16,580 --> 00:23:16,860
Hmm.

415
00:23:18,060 --> 00:23:19,380
Let's make something to eat.

416
00:23:19,380 --> 00:23:25,220
You know, I understand now why Senchi starts cooking all of a sudden.

417
00:23:26,020 --> 00:23:29,100
In this body, I get hungry faster than before.

418
00:23:29,840 --> 00:23:34,060
You say that, but I've never seen Namari start cooking full meals out of nowhere.

419
00:23:34,940 --> 00:23:35,100
Hmm.

420
00:23:35,440 --> 00:23:38,220
Cooking is simply what I do while I'm self-reflecting.

421
00:23:38,220 --> 00:23:42,680
Take flour, water, salt, and eggs, and knead them together.

422
00:23:43,400 --> 00:23:44,380
Then let it rest.

423
00:23:45,080 --> 00:23:49,340
While you're waiting, add some chopped up onions and other vegetables to the minced meat,

424
00:23:49,460 --> 00:23:51,060
and mix it all up.

425
00:23:51,480 --> 00:23:53,340
Make a cylinder out of the rested dough,

426
00:23:53,880 --> 00:23:55,220
cut into equal parts,

427
00:23:55,880 --> 00:23:57,080
and roll flat.

428
00:23:58,080 --> 00:24:01,320
Put the filling on the flattened dough, and then...

429
00:24:01,320 --> 00:24:01,620
wrap.

430
00:24:01,620 --> 00:24:13,720
How odd.

431
00:24:14,360 --> 00:24:17,920
Preparing the food in silence like that really helped me calm down.

432
00:24:18,200 --> 00:24:19,920
I think we went a little overkill.

433
00:24:19,920 --> 00:24:21,480
They turned out well, huh?

434
00:24:25,560 --> 00:24:26,620
It's ready.

435
00:24:29,440 --> 00:24:31,560
The shape of it is pretty familiar.

436
00:24:31,880 --> 00:24:34,180
But it's weird, because it doesn't smell like it should.

437
00:24:34,420 --> 00:24:36,640
You've never had them with potatoes or cheese?

438
00:24:36,980 --> 00:24:39,000
These are typically fried from where I'm from.

439
00:24:39,680 --> 00:24:41,300
Now it's time to dig in.

440
00:24:44,260 --> 00:24:45,200
Be careful.

441
00:24:45,600 --> 00:24:47,080
Otherwise, you'll burn yourself.

442
00:24:47,180 --> 00:24:48,000
Oh, you think?

443
00:24:48,600 --> 00:24:50,000
Oh, this is good.

444
00:24:50,240 --> 00:24:51,940
Strangely, almost better than normal.

445
00:24:52,360 --> 00:24:54,800
Did changing races affect our taste buds, too?

446
00:24:55,540 --> 00:24:56,020
No.

447
00:24:56,400 --> 00:24:58,140
These are good no matter who's eating them.

448
00:24:58,780 --> 00:24:59,700
Strange, isn't it?

449
00:24:59,700 --> 00:25:03,440
Every region and race makes their dumplings in completely different ways.

450
00:25:03,620 --> 00:25:05,600
But in the end, they're all still delicious.

451
00:25:06,860 --> 00:25:07,960
Yeah, that's right.

452
00:25:09,120 --> 00:25:11,280
That basically applies to all of us, too.

453
00:25:11,440 --> 00:25:14,780
Even though we've changed a little bit, we're still just the same person in the end.

454
00:25:15,200 --> 00:25:16,360
We're gonna make it work.

455
00:25:16,960 --> 00:25:19,160
Well, I guess that wraps everything up now.

456
00:25:19,720 --> 00:25:20,880
Yeah, in your head, maybe.

457
00:25:20,880 --> 00:25:24,700
Anyway, this place is so unique.

458
00:25:24,700 --> 00:25:26,180
What exactly is it?

459
00:25:26,320 --> 00:25:29,540
It's basically a type of defensive point that the dwarves built.

460
00:25:30,060 --> 00:25:30,960
Defensive point?

461
00:25:31,520 --> 00:25:34,000
It's from back when the elves and dwarves were in a war.

462
00:25:34,400 --> 00:25:36,280
You didn't learn about this in school?

463
00:25:36,660 --> 00:25:41,700
Both sides battled in an arms race to make more advanced technology, which ended up being catastrophic.

464
00:25:41,700 --> 00:25:49,620
Ever since, the dwarves and elves have feared that history would eventually repeat itself, so they've limited technology use inside the dungeons.

465
00:25:50,300 --> 00:25:57,300
The conflict between races was especially intense within this dungeon, so there will be a lot of disputes when it comes to acquiring it.

466
00:25:57,300 --> 00:26:03,560
Yeah, well, regarding that, if the elves happen to come after us, you'll be able to do something to fix it, right?

467
00:26:04,020 --> 00:26:05,440
Huh? Wait, why me?

468
00:26:05,560 --> 00:26:10,100
You must have connections! Your mother was a court magician! You told us that, didn't you?

469
00:26:10,180 --> 00:26:11,660
I mean, yeah, I did, but...

470
00:26:11,660 --> 00:26:14,860
Calm down. Either way, she's a half-foot at the moment.

471
00:26:15,520 --> 00:26:17,800
If anybody talks with the elves, it's him.

472
00:26:20,340 --> 00:26:21,900
I shall do my best.

473
00:26:23,520 --> 00:26:26,800
Let's find a way to get us all back to normal as soon as possible, yeah?

474
00:26:27,300 --> 00:26:28,480
Agreed.

